import{_ as n,d as a,e as t,x as i}from"./chunks/framework.BRr8VP3a.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"D.09 Love, Care, Recognition, Meaning, and Quality of Life","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"D.09 Love, Care, Recognition, Meaning, and Quality of Life","xkChars":0,"xkWords":481},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/theory/appendix-d/d-09.md","filePath":"en/theory/appendix-d/d-09.md"}'),o={name:"en/theory/appendix-d/d-09.md"};function s(r,e,d,l,c,p){return a(),t("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[i('<div class="theory-source"><h1 id="section-d-09" tabindex="-1"><span class="xk-num"><span class="xk-num__n">D.09</span><span class="xk-num__gap"></span></span>Love, Care, Recognition, Meaning, and Quality of Life <a class="header-anchor" href="#section-d-09" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;D.09 Love, Care, Recognition, Meaning, and Quality of Life {#section-d-09}&quot;">​</a></h1><p>In the main text, see §1.8, §7.3.11, §9.7, §14.3, and Appendix A.11. Research entries cover 09.01–09.09.</p><p>Love can be an experience, a relationship, an action, or a normative understanding. Care can involve identifying needs, taking up the work, carrying it out, and responding. Recognition concerns standing, respect, and life together. Their shared concern with people does not make them a single functional variable. Private companionship, quietly watching, rest, hope, or mourning need not produce a detectable change in group structure to be meaningful.</p><p>Voluntariness, fairness, capability, and outcomes require separate evidence. Someone’s willingness to help does not establish a fair distribution of burdens. Low-cost help can still express goodwill, and considerable effort does not establish that refusal was freely available. HV11 is used to describe a particular bounded undertaking and its conditional consequences. It supplies neither a definition of all love nor a scale for judging personality from cost.</p><p>Death, dispersal, the end of a relationship, and organizational exit concern different objects and clocks. The end of a legal relationship, restoration of living arrangements, and changes in mourning can occur at different times. Organizational X0 cannot be applied as a model of a person’s death or universal stages of grief. Hope can support action, but wishes about the future, probability judgments, plans, and revisable commitments still have to be kept separate.</p><p>In a teaching example, direct contact may have to stop when someone leaves a relationship, while children or other dependents still need care to continue safely. Continuity of care cannot justify forcing someone who has been harmed to remain exposed. A justified exit also does not remove the need to check bounded duties that have independent grounds. Well-being, dignity, freedom from harm, and meaning can be evaluated alongside one another. People must not be compelled to accept a total score that decides every aspect of their lives for them.</p><p>Taking up the work of helping someone may involve doing a task, noticing needs, arranging, reminding, checking, and being on call. Completing one task can be genuine help. A claim that it reduces the burden over time also requires checking who does the coordination work. The fact that someone else can do the work does not make the person loved replaceable. Fewer tasks need not take away the sense of loss. An undertaking remains eligible to be described and evaluated even if it does not have the intended consequences.</p><p>Research topics. 09.01 Love as experience, relationship, and action. 09.02 Care ethics (Gilligan, Tronto, and others). 09.03 Recognition, dignity, and intersubjectivity (Hegel, Honneth, and others). 09.04 Existentialism, the absurd, and meaning (Kierkegaard, Sartre, Camus, Frankl, and others). 09.05 Death, mourning, memory, and endings. 09.06 Sacrifice, gifts, devotion, and depletion of the self. 09.07 Hope, faith, commitment, and the future. 09.08 Loneliness, belonging, friendship, and intimacy. 09.09 Suffering, happiness, desire, and quality of life.</p></div>',1)])])}const g=n(o,[["render",s]]);export{u as __pageData,g as default};
